# Manually transcribed by OWID from p. 626: the share of all children under 16 in the wool town of
# Tilburg who had an occupational registration, in 1849 and 1899. Because the denominator includes
# children aged 0-9, these rates are far below those measured on a 10-14 base.
# In case of updating, upload manually.

# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "The world of child labor. An historical and regional survey"
    description: |-
      A reference work surveying the history of child labor region by region, with contributions from child labor scholars, researchers, policy-makers and activists, together with statistical data.

      The figures taken from it here come from the chapter on the Netherlands and cover the wool town of Tilburg: the share of all children under the age of sixteen with an occupational registration in 1849 and in 1899.
    date_published: "2009"

    # Citation
    producer: Hindman
    citation_full: |-
      van Nederveen Meerkerk, E. (2009). History of child labor in the Netherlands. In H. D. Hindman (Ed.), The world of child labor. An historical and regional survey (p. 626). Routledge.

    # Files
